{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure","id":1244197,"title":"2e: Purity Crucible Strike, how comes Dragon Bloods ain't pure ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-09T10:35:46-07:00","id":1244197,"title":"2e: Purity Crucible Strike, how comes Dragon Bloods ain't pure ?","content":"Reading this charm makes me think of the implications of it, how comes first age solars didn't mass breed and used this charm as a way to obtain millions of dragon blooded retainers ?<br /> <br /> Step 1 Order your slave/servant DB to mass produce with the brainwashed population of your principality, everyone gets a DB kid.<br /> Step 2 Use Terrestrial Edification Program to rise the presence of your older DB to 6 and tell them to learn the charm<br /> Step 3 wait a few centuries while you indoctrinate the low breeding DB and keep producing more, use TEP to rise one of their virtues so they can channel them.<br /> Step 4 wait 100/200 years or so so they can rise their essence to an acceptable level, mass use PCS to rise their breeding. Sure some will die but by rising their essence and virtue channeling you can keep it to moderate numbers, and if you have millions of them....<br /> Step 5 Profit<br /> In less than a millenia you'll have as much dragon blooded as you want, a steady influx of them that will keep getting their blood purified to be completely pure breed DBs and soon you will need humans no more... except perhaps to save you from the very DB you've created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","user":"Cruzwindt","date":". 08-09-2018, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","name":"Cruzwindt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T11:05:19-07:00","id":1244208,"title":"","content":"Congratulations,you've discovered one of the many ways 2e devalued every non-Solar Exalt, which is like finding a straw of hay in a haystack.<br /> <br /> The ostensible reason, if you insist on one, could be as simple as &quot;You can't force me.&quot;<br /> [DB] So wait, you want me to punch purity into my own brothers and sisters, murdering plenty of them, so that... you can have a <i>slightly</i> fancier army than your neighbor?<br /> [Solar] YES.<br /> [DB] Right. I'll get right on that. BRB I have a meeting to get to with a sidereal about a ... surpation-uyay....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 08-09-2018, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":22}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T11:32:43-07:00","id":1244220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244208#post1244208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Congratulations,you've discovered one of the many ways 2e devalued every non-Solar Exalt, which is like finding a straw of hay in a haystack.<br /> <br /> The ostensible reason, if you insist on one, could be as simple as &quot;You can't force me.&quot;<br /> [DB] So wait, you want me to punch purity into my own brothers and sisters, murdering plenty of them, so that... you can have a <i>slightly</i> fancier army than your neighbor?<br /> [Solar] YES.<br /> [DB] Right. I'll get right on that. BRB I have a meeting to get to with a sidereal about a ... surpation-uyay....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I logged in for the first time in a year solely to give you a like and acknowledge you made me laugh out loud. Well done. <br /> <br /> Slightly more seriously, there's two versions of Exalted especially in 2e. There's the Exalted you read about in the lore, the setting detail and the history. And then there's the rules engine. Ideally, most games want to synch the two up so there's minimal disconnect. 2e didn't do an especially good job of that. You will inevitably find ways to break the setting. Try to think of it as a feature rather than a bug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11870-epiphany","name":"Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T11:41:27-07:00","id":1244228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244208#post1244208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Congratulations,you've discovered one of the many ways 2e devalued every non-Solar Exalt, which is like finding a straw of hay in a haystack.<br /> <br /> The ostensible reason, if you insist on one, could be as simple as &quot;You can't force me.&quot;<br /> [DB] So wait, you want me to punch purity into my own brothers and sisters, murdering plenty of them, so that... you can have a <i>slightly</i> fancier army than your neighbor?<br /> [Solar] YES.<br /> [DB] Right. I'll get right on that. BRB I have a meeting to get to with a sidereal about a ... surpation-uyay....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> LOL That answer. Despite being so funny, it's actually a great idea for an usurpation game.... Solar gets betrayed by the millions of dragon blood slaves he had made attempting to create a nation of only exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","name":"Cruzwindt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T11:44:52-07:00","id":1244230,"title":"","content":"Really, most questions about &quot;Why didn't this happen&quot; can be answered by stepping back and asking: Are you inquiring about the setting as perceived by an omniscient, all-knowing, perfectly prescient and sage genius who knows everything you have ever read in any book ever? A Perfect Rational Actor whose every action is driven towards optimization of some goal?<br /> <br /> If so, stop that. The Exalted of the First Age squabbled, adventured, warred, reveled, loved, and wept. They built empires, forged wonders, united kingdoms, made fortunes, and generally did a lot of Really Cool Adventure stuff.<br /> <br /> They were not nerds who sat around thinking on the most efficient way to optimize dragon-blooded breeding for maximum output, and even if they were, and I realize that 2e did not encourage this idea, <b><i>the Dragon-Blooded were also Exalted</i></b>. They had squabbles and adventures and wars and revelries and love triangles and sorrows to attend to! They built their own kingdoms, forged wonders of their own, became rich beyond mortal imagining, and did their own Really Cool Adventure stuff, even if it was slightly less Epic and Mythic by dint of being limited by their lesser power relative to the Solars.<br /> <br /> 2e seems to have given you the impression that the Dragon-Blooded were mindless slaves devotedly loyal to the Solars, willing to spend their entire 500 year lifespans meditating on mountains and focusing their essence to take a gamble at dying in order to become marginally more powerful.<br /> <br /> If this is true, 2e was wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T15:25:28-07:00","id":1244294,"title":"","content":"Shortly after Glories to the Most High came out I came to the conclusion that it and DotFA were actually the wrong way around.<br /> <br /> Glories is an excellent framework for a world where the Incanae still took an interest in things and were actively worshiped and many of the charms introduced were referencing the excesses of First Age Exalts while DotFA was more interested in the crazy power of high essence even if the setting it'd created for First Age Solars couldn't really stand up to them running around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T18:16:42-07:00","id":1244336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244230#post1244230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, most questions about &quot;Why didn't this happen&quot; can be answered by stepping back and asking: Are you inquiring about the setting as perceived by an omniscient, all-knowing, perfectly prescient and sage genius who knows everything you have ever read in any book ever? A Perfect Rational Actor whose every action is driven towards optimization of some goal?<br /> <br /> If so, stop that. The Exalted of the First Age squabbled, adventured, warred, reveled, loved, and wept. They built empires, forged wonders, united kingdoms, made fortunes, and generally did a lot of Really Cool Adventure stuff.<br /> <br /> They were not nerds who sat around thinking on the most efficient way to optimize dragon-blooded breeding for maximum output, and even if they were, and I realize that 2e did not encourage this idea, <b><i>the Dragon-Blooded were also Exalted</i></b>. They had squabbles and adventures and wars and revelries and love triangles and sorrows to attend to! They built their own kingdoms, forged wonders of their own, became rich beyond mortal imagining, and did their own Really Cool Adventure stuff, even if it was slightly less Epic and Mythic by dint of being limited by their lesser power relative to the Solars.<br /> <br /> 2e seems to have given you the impression that the Dragon-Blooded were mindless slaves devotedly loyal to the Solars, willing to spend their entire 500 year lifespans meditating on mountains and focusing their essence to take a gamble at dying in order to become marginally more powerful.<br /> <br /> If this is true, 2e was wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not mindless, but unknowing slaves nonetheless.<br /> Drams of the First Age portrays Dragon Blooded as very loyal, and only after many centuries their faith in the solars started to fade, also, they are supposed to get around a thousand years of lifespan if they take care of themselves, and since there has been 3000 years in the age of dreams, and the usurpation went around 4000-5000 years since the primordial war, there hasn't been that many generations of DBs since then, at least in 2e, one that lived the primordial war is even alive , Gauto I think.<br /> <br /> Now, we can't argue which portrayal of the Dbs is better, since that is pretty much relative to every person's subjective tastes.<br /> <br /> But we can do talk about why they SHOULDN'T be portrayed as loyal fanatical servants to the side of their solar masters, who had a lot of brainwashing and mind altering charms, and indoctrinated them since birth as per their role of generals-army commanders.<br /> We must take note, that 2e doesn't portray all DBs in that light, in fact, some of them even mildly rebelled against their solar masters, refusing to serve their master's reincarnations and creating their own gentes to serve another purpose besides being an army for their superiors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","user":"Cruzwindt","date":". 08-09-2018, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","name":"Cruzwindt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T18:40:02-07:00","id":1244340,"title":"","content":"No, 2e was pretty much objectively, undeniably wrong in painting them as slaves and boosting up Solars to the point where they could brainwash someone by saying &quot;hi&quot; with no recourse to resist, but then, this is the 2e social system being a heap of manure [comparable to most social systems but still terrible].<br /> <br /> This was a consequence of 2e essentially designing most systems so Solar charms were required for baseline competence and no one else was able to match Solars [and thus have baseline competence], which transformed all competitions from where they should have been, the equivalent of a footrace between Flash and Superman [both are really really fast but there's a definite winner] into a footrace between three pretty fast athletes [the three Solaroids], two people hand-walking without legs [sidereals and lunars], and one violently twitching quadriplegic torso [DBs].","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T19:23:19-07:00","id":1244347,"title":"","content":"Well I will not, and can't, argue that the social combat system of 2ed is good, it was BAD. I see what they were trying to do, make a system which allows to actually convince others instead of conversation being merely plot lines. But they did it wrong.<br /> I'm talking more about the fluff of how 2ed portrays DBs. Also you cannot convince everyone of everything, since their motivation protects them from many things.<br /> <br /> So, why shouldn't the beings created to be the soldiers of the solars, not be at their command ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","user":"Cruzwindt","date":". 08-09-2018, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","name":"Cruzwindt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T19:51:16-07:00","id":1244352,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12433\" data-vbnamecard=\"12433\">Cruzwindt</a> because that deprotagonizes the Dragonblooded. It renders them nothing but NPC\u2019s whose lives are at the whim of Solars. This is again as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar756_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"756\" data-vbnamecard=\"756\">Meianno Yuurei</a> points out one of the big problems with 2e DBs from their 1E or 3e counterparts. It reduces their prominence in the story of Creation to make it literally impossible to really tell compelling stories with Dragonblooded and any solaroid splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T01:12:03-07:00","id":1244410,"title":"","content":"Even by Second Edition standards, people of that mindset would not reach Essence 6.<br /> <br /> I mean, people of a much more independent mindset are probably not often getting higher than Essence 4 either, but that's a whole other thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T03:05:09-07:00","id":1244431,"title":"","content":"Yep, that's the answer. The scheme fails in step 4 when the dragonblooded become enlightened enough to go &quot;what the fuck am I doing&quot; and fuck off to do their own thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T04:10:01-07:00","id":1244441,"title":"","content":"This is also the kind of thing that might make other Celestial Exalts take pre-emptive action against you because this is the behaviour of someone who intends to make a massive power grab.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T07:23:33-07:00","id":1244480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244410#post1244410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even by Second Edition standards, people of that mindset would not reach Essence 6.<br /> <br /> I mean, people of a much more independent mindset are probably not often getting higher than Essence 4 either, but that's a whole other thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I get what you're saying, but I think that you have too high standards for 2ed then, I remember a few character DBs with that mindset with essence 5 lol.<br /> <br /> Then again, protagonism is a weird think to talk about that's most of it in the GM of the game and in the kind of story you're playing. The power level and capacity of it seems a little irrelevant to that in my opinion. A Player character DB doesn't have to be any less protagonist than a Solar, on certain kind of games.<br /> Dragon Bloods have always been the numberless kinds of exalted , there can be as many dragon blood as the setting needs for, and that's been since 1ed if I'm not wrong. It's hard to think that there are any numbers of protagonists having their impact on the worlds at the same time.<br /> <br /> Sorry but it's hard to understand the individualism- level of protagonist concept for me. I don't see that much correlation between the two. The less individualistic character can be a protagonist starting off his own adventures, and vice versa, the most individualistic characters can be NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","name":"Cruzwindt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T07:34:43-07:00","id":1244485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cruzwindt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244480#post1244480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I get what you're saying, but I think that you have too high standards for 2ed then, I remember a few character DBs with that mindset with essence 5 lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be interested in hearing more about this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cruzwindt</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, protagonism is a weird think to talk about that's most of it in the GM of the game and in the kind of story you're playing. The power level and capacity of it seems a little irrelevant to that in my opinion. A Player character DB doesn't have to be any less protagonist than a Solar, on certain kind of games.<br /> Dragon Bloods have always been the numberless kinds of exalted , there can be as many dragon blood as the setting needs for, and that's been since 1ed if I'm not wrong. It's hard to think that there are any numbers of protagonists having their impact on the worlds at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like a much stronger argument against having thousands of people with Essence 6.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T07:39:19-07:00","id":1244490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244441#post1244441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is also the kind of thing that might make other Celestial Exalts take pre-emptive action against you because this is the behaviour of someone who intends to make a massive power grab.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And as it's a plan that takes hundreds of years, there's plenty of opportunity to a)find out, and b)stop it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T07:49:00-07:00","id":1244493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cruzwindt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244347#post1244347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, why shouldn't the beings created to be the soldiers of the solars, not be at their command ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I refer you back to &quot;2e was wrong&quot;. 2e smeared shit all over itself by its' efforts to deprotagonize everyone but Solars. Arguing about why 2e did or didn't do something is an inherently fruitless endeavor because it all stems back to &quot;2e was wrong&quot;. <br /> <br /> &quot;Why shouldn't the soldiers--&quot;<br /> Soldiers choose to obey. Loyalty is earned. And these are Exalted nonetheless. You seem to think that soldier = slave.<br /> <br /> A general can order his soldier to march, to fight. The soldier will obey because these are reasonable, rational orders, which he agreed to follow. <br /> <br /> If a general orders his soldier to abandon their wife and marry someone else because of superior breeding outcomes, the soldier is fully within their rights to say &quot;the hell you say&quot;. They are not a slave. Their personal lives are voluntarily set aside for service, but are not for the general to dictate.<br /> <br /> And again, these soldiers are <i>Exalted</i>. If that doesn't mean anything to you...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T08:21:23-07:00","id":1244502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244493#post1244493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I refer you back to &quot;2e was wrong&quot;. 2e smeared shit all over itself by its' efforts to deprotagonize everyone but Solars. Arguing about why 2e did or didn't do something is an inherently fruitless endeavor because it all stems back to &quot;2e was wrong&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why shouldn't the soldiers--&quot;<br /> Soldiers choose to obey. Loyalty is earned. And these are Exalted nonetheless. You seem to think that soldier = slave.<br /> <br /> A general can order his soldier to march, to fight. The soldier will obey because these are reasonable, rational orders, which he agreed to follow.<br /> <br /> If a general orders his soldier to abandon their wife and marry someone else because of superior breeding outcomes, the soldier is fully within their rights to say &quot;the hell you say&quot;. They are not a slave. Their personal lives are voluntarily set aside for service, but are not for the general to dictate.<br /> <br /> And again, these soldiers are <i>Exalted</i>. If that doesn't mean anything to you...</div> </div> </div> </div>One issue there. History is replete with examples of people committing atrocities because 'they were just following orders.' You can take a random person off the street and get them to torture someone because there's a person with a lab coat telling them it's okay and that they should keep going. <br /> <br /> Authority is a scary thing.<br /> <br /> That said, history is <i>also </i> replete with examples of individuals who ignored their orders to try and do the right thing or to do what they felt was right. If only 1/10 mortals are willing to break from the mold and refuse to conform, I'd think that it would be more like 9/10 Dragon Bloods who do. Because Every. Single. One. Of. Them. is a god damn hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T08:22:19-07:00","id":1244503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244485#post1244485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be interested in hearing more about this.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they were 3, Saibok Gauto who remains a loyal soldier primordial war survivor, he was essence 9-8 if I remember right.<br /> Then the other two were essence 5, one a DB in the Deliberative Armada who remained loyal to the solars, because he knew they were needed to protect creation. He also was considering murdering one of his children cuz she didn't exalted and he was worried that would ruin his military career.<br /> And the other was Anjei who was literally a slave. They are in the end fo Dreams of the First Age Lords of Creation supplement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244485#post1244485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems like a much stronger argument against having thousands of people with Essence 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>mmm you're right, it may be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244493#post1244493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Why shouldn't the soldiers--&quot;<br /> Soldiers choose to obey. Loyalty is earned. And these are Exalted nonetheless. You seem to think that soldier = slave.<br /> <br /> A general can order his soldier to march, to fight. The soldier will obey because these are reasonable, rational orders, which he agreed to follow.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but you are forgetting that these soldiers are indoctrinated since birth, if we can get anything from how the primordial war went off, is that the Dragon Blooded of first generation concentrated in reproducing. or else there couldn't be many left, specially with a war that killed people all around creation.<br /> They were also made for the purpose of being liutenants of the celestials and put at their command. Only after years of abuses and excess did that loyalty worn off and they betrayed their masters. But before that they were mostly loyal to them.<br /> <br /> Also, many soldiers don't necessarily follow rational orders as per following their conscience. If that would be true then war crimes wouldn't exist.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244493#post1244493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If a general orders his soldier to abandon their wife and marry someone else because of superior breeding outcomes, the soldier is fully within their rights to say &quot;the hell you say&quot;. They are not a slave. Their personal lives are voluntarily set aside for service, but are not for the general to dictate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course and as portrayed in DoTFA many did so, but many other did not, because since child they were told that the moral thing to do was obey solars.<br /> Again, it's hard to me to see why does this takes protagonism from the DBs. A soldier can be a hero despite not being a general.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244493#post1244493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And again, these soldiers are <i>Exalted</i>. If that doesn't mean anything to you...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we don't have to have the same concepts for everything, I'm just trying to understand which one gives the maximum output of fun. But I don't see correlation between the things you say.<br /> Just because there is someone more powerful than you and that person can manipulate you into doing things doesn't make you less of a protagonist, in fact, many good histories go down that way, with the heroes being manipulated into helping the bad guy achieve ultimate power and then defeating him with a McGuffin or some other thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","user":"Cruzwindt","date":". 08-10-2018, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","name":"Cruzwindt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T08:25:32-07:00","id":1244507,"title":"","content":"Hey, maybe a bunch of Solars did decide to do it. And that was one of the contributing factors behind the Usurpation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T08:28:19-07:00","id":1244508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244493#post1244493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A general can order his soldier to march, to fight. The soldier will obey because these are reasonable, rational orders, which he agreed to follow.<br /> <br /> If a general orders his soldier to abandon their wife and marry someone else because of superior breeding outcomes, the soldier is fully within their rights to say &quot;the hell you say&quot;. They are not a slave. Their personal lives are voluntarily set aside for service, but are not for the general to dictate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should say, this kind of thing does sometimes happen. People can be pressured by society to divorce and remarry. My dad has a colleague who was fired+blacklisted in the USSR from his job as a physicist because he got ordained, and his wife was &quot;encouraged&quot; to divorce him, or she'd be blacklisted too (and so she did divorce him, which he didn't really blame her for).<br /> <br /> And in the Roman Empire, nobles (optimates, equestrians, etc, I mean) were sometimes told to get divorces and remarry by the head of their households, for political position or wealth or whatever.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say that you're entirely wrong. I mean, I could imagine a Solar ordering his Dragonblood to do it. But it'd surely make them pretty pissed off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-10-2018, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T08:38:33-07:00","id":1244514,"title":"","content":"The difference is that you seem to hold it as <i><b>the default</b></i> that every single DB should have been a brainwashed little slave to their Solar Masters. I think part of this is heavily the fact that 2e mechanics were absolute shit -- I usually define it like so:<br /> <br /> 100% is the baseline capacity required to interact with the systems, other than &quot;killing a dude&quot;.<br /> 2e Solars have 100-120%.<br /> 2e Lunars and Sidereals are in the 60-70% range. 2e DBs in the 30% range, Mortals down around 10%.<br /> <br /> As such of COURSE DBs look like utter trash who should be effortlessly twisted around Solar fingers, they're so shitty, they have shitty shitshit worthless charms compared to Solars who actually function.<br /> <br /> 3e makes it more like100% mortals, 160% DBs, 200% Solars. Solars are amazing, and more powerful. But DBs function, they're cool and capable and can actually act. On top of this, the social influence system is more robust and functional, so it's not so simple as &quot;Brainwashing is just a matter of draining their Willpower to 0 so they can't resist and then influencing them however you like and oh of course Solars are the best at draining WP and pushing people so of course they'd be able to just effortlessly brainwash everyone around them into being perfect little slaves who do whatever they say and it doesn't even take all that much effort for them teehee one Solar can totally effortlessly brainwash 100,000 DBs.&quot;<br /> <br /> I believe that if, as you seem to hold, 99% of DBs are docile little lamb-slaves who happily throw themselves into the grinder for a marginal increase of power at the behest of their Solar masters, dying by the thousands to try and make a &quot;more pure&quot; bloodline for a few extra motes here and there, then yeah, they've had their agency and protagonism fully stripped away.<br /> <br /> 2e also painted Creation's First Age as perfectly divided up into three hundred solar domains where each was LAW and there was nowhere that was not a Solar domain for someone to act on their own because they were all unified in some pan-Creation harmonious government. 3e paints the first age as a long, tumultuous time in which they had strife against each other and the world, striving to claim the vast reaches of Creation in the wake of the victory of the gods and their Chosen, not some &quot;boom, done&quot; thing. There was no panopticon-style &quot;all within this territory know obedience to their Solar Master&quot;, Dragon-Blooded and Lunars could easily set out and claim places for themselves, creating their own principalities and kingdoms, their own dynasties that swore allegiance to no Solar.<br /> <br /> This is better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T09:31:56-07:00","id":1244523,"title":"","content":"Don't forget, Most dragon blooded who'd learn the charm probably view any dilution of the blood of the Dragons as blasphemy.<br /> <br /> That further makes this plan a BAD idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T11:37:06-07:00","id":1244581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244514#post1244514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference is that you seem to hold it as <i><b>the default</b></i> that every single DB should have been a brainwashed little slave to their Solar Masters. I think part of this is heavily the fact that 2e mechanics were absolute shit -- I usually define it like so:</div> </div> </div> </div>No no, I don't, as I've said before, there were many free DBs on the 1st Age 2ed setting. Entire gentes refused to serve their Solar's reincarnations. But Solars from the first millenia after the PW were extremely powerful, those were the ones who had a tight hold on the gentes they were given.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244514#post1244514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">100% is the baseline capacity required to interact with the systems, other than &quot;killing a dude&quot;.<br /> 2e Solars have 100-120%.<br /> 2e Lunars and Sidereals are in the 60-70% range. 2e DBs in the 30% range, Mortals down around 10%.<br /> <br /> As such of COURSE DBs look like utter trash who should be effortlessly twisted around Solar fingers, they're so shitty, they have shitty shitshit worthless charms compared to Solars who actually function.<br /> <br /> 3e makes it more like100% mortals, 160% DBs, 200% Solars. Solars are amazing, and more powerful. But DBs function, they're cool and capable and can actually act. On top of this, the social influence system is more robust and functional, so it's not so simple as &quot;Brainwashing is just a matter of draining their Willpower to 0 so they can't resist and then influencing them however you like and oh of course Solars are the best at draining WP and pushing people so of course they'd be able to just effortlessly brainwash everyone around them into being perfect little slaves who do whatever they say and it doesn't even take all that much effort for them teehee one Solar can totally effortlessly brainwash 100,000 DBs.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well I disagree there, a game that has all ''classes'' balanced so anyone can pick any race or class they like and still have fun together, so that a human can be on the same level as the doom race created from the ashes of titans and dragon fire with the power of angels and demons, it's great for some people, but personally I don't find balance that interesting, I've had more fun in games that are not balanced, either being an OP character that does shenanigans, or a small being trying to overthrow a very powerful existence in an almost impossible campaign.<br /> Also lorewise, if the different Exalteds didn't had that much difference in power, it would make the whole point of solars useless. Why spend all that power making a few hundred warriors who are just slightly better, when you can simply create thousands more who are almost as good and even reproduce ?<br /> <br /> Also you can't Brainwash anyone as per rules, after all, you cannot make someone go against their motivation without unnatural influence, and that fades off quite quick, unless we are talking about Threefold binding of the heart, which was a 1ed spell btw, and combined with Imbue Amalgan you can easily brainwash hundreds of people.<br /> The REAL problem with 2ed social combat ain't brainwashing, but that you can break the system to NATURALLY compel people to do your bidding, so, it's no that you brainwashed someone, but more that you REALLY convinced them to murder their wife and children. Which makes little to no sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244514#post1244514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that if, as you seem to hold, 99% of DBs are docile little lamb-slaves who happily throw themselves into the grinder for a marginal increase of power at the behest of their Solar masters, dying by the thousands to try and make a &quot;more pure&quot; bloodline for a few extra motes here and there, then yeah, they've had their agency and protagonism fully stripped away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you say that being at the solar's service makes them less of a protagonist, but I don't see that way. A DB can be as much of a hero ( in the greek sense of the word ) as he wants while still being at the command of a superior. Most of the time, the adventurer that goes to kill the demon king does so at the behest of a King who orders him to. That doesn't make the adventurer less of the protagonist of that history.<br /> Also, DBs serfdom has little to do with being docile, and more with the fact that their creator made them with the purpose of being under Solar's care, and like the solars who evolved from being Titan killing machines into kings, the DBs also evolved from that purpose in the future, but the 1st age BEFORE the usurpation, was a time before that evolution happen, so I don't see the problem with them still being loyal to their commanders in chief.<br /> <br /> From a mortal perspective this may make sense, but we are talking from the perspectives of beings that live hundreds of years.<br /> <br /> Younger DB: Hey grandfather, remember those histories you told us about how the solars saved the world and even your life during the primordial war ?<br /> Elder DB: Sure kid, want me to tell them again for you ?<br /> Younger DB: nah, I just wanted to tell you we are going to revolt and kill all the solars, wanna join old man ?<br /> Elder DB: What ?!<br /> <br /> At the time, many DBs had their trust earned by the solars, even if they manipulated them for that trust. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244514#post1244514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2e also painted Creation's First Age as perfectly divided up into three hundred solar domains where each was LAW and there was nowhere that was not a Solar domain for someone to act on their own because they were all unified in some pan-Creation harmonious government. 3e paints the first age as a long, tumultuous time in which they had strife against each other and the world, striving to claim the vast reaches of Creation in the wake of the victory of the gods and their Chosen, not some &quot;boom, done&quot; thing. There was no panopticon-style &quot;all within this territory know obedience to their Solar Master&quot;, Dragon-Blooded and Lunars could easily set out and claim places for themselves, creating their own principalities and kingdoms, their own dynasties that swore allegiance to no Solar.<br /> <br /> This is better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's untrue, sure the 1st age is portrayed as a very peaceful time for humanity. But there weren't 300 domains, only a few solars had actually principalities, most of them just had manses and lands in their care. The solars actually fought one another in less of an open war and most in assassination, defamation , etcs. It was more of a cold war era. There were a lot of times of war before the age of dreams with open warfare between the solars, but eventually the most powerful faction of the deliberative brought an end to the conflict. Which I don't see nothing wrong with. After all, creation was given to the solars, not to other exalteds, it would make little sense for anyone to oppose the saviors of the world, and the gods themselves who rule it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","user":"Cruzwindt","date":". 08-10-2018, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","name":"Cruzwindt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T15:47:30-07:00","id":1244646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cruzwindt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244581#post1244581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, you say that being at the solar's service makes them less of a protagonist, but I don't see that way. A DB can be as much of a hero ( in the greek sense of the word ) as he wants while still being at the command of a superior. Most of the time, the adventurer that goes to kill the demon king does so at the behest of a King who orders him to. That doesn't make the adventurer less of the protagonist of that history.<br /> Also, DBs serfdom has little to do with being docile, and more with the fact that their creator made them with the purpose of being under Solar's care, and like the solars who evolved from being Titan killing machines into kings, the DBs also evolved from that purpose in the future, but the 1st age BEFORE the usurpation, was a time before that evolution happen, so I don't see the problem with them still being loyal to their commanders in chief.<br /> <br /> From a mortal perspective this may make sense, but we are talking from the perspectives of beings that live hundreds of years.<br /> <br /> Younger DB: Hey grandfather, remember those histories you told us about how the solars saved the world and even your life during the primordial war ?<br /> Elder DB: Sure kid, want me to tell them again for you ?<br /> Younger DB: nah, I just wanted to tell you we are going to revolt and kill all the solars, wanna join old man ?<br /> Elder DB: What ?!<br /> <br /> At the time, many DBs had their trust earned by the solars, even if they manipulated them for that trust.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>How many stories are there where the hero blindly obeyed the king, did the quest and both the hero and the king were protagonists of the story? I think you'll find that in the majority of those stories, either the king is just a quest giver NPC who doesn't really ask the hero to do anything unheroic, ever, or the king tries to manipulate the hero, making him an antagonist for the hero to overcome. I can think of a couple that do go along the lines you say, but they pretty much all involve a hero ordering his loyal dog to do things. And as awesome as dogs are, 'you are playing someone's pet' isn't exactly the best first step to get most players into the mindset of exalted gaming. Even Pugmire doesn't make you play pets.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T16:57:14-07:00","id":1244665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244646#post1244646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How many stories are there where the hero blindly obeyed the king, did the quest and both the hero and the king were protagonists of the story? I think you'll find that in the majority of those stories, either the king is just a quest giver NPC who doesn't really ask the hero to do anything unheroic, ever, or the king tries to manipulate the hero, making him an antagonist for the hero to overcome. I can think of a couple that do go along the lines you say, but they pretty much all involve a hero ordering his loyal dog to do things. And as awesome as dogs are, 'you are playing someone's pet' isn't exactly the best first step to get most players into the mindset of exalted gaming. Even Pugmire doesn't make you play pets.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno if we can post links in this forum but <br /> <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/UnwittingPawn\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.p.../UnwittingPawn</a><br /> What can I say dude, it's a pretty common thing for a protagonistic character to be manipulated into something. <br /> <br /> And I get what you are saying, but , the moment a player characer starts playing out a DB, it stops being someone's pet, and starts getting that much deserved individualism we were talking about back there. There are ways to escape solar brainwashing through plot and other ways around it, but you need to be a Player Character or a plot convergence to do so. It's not impossible just really hard. But saying that DBs should be slightly less powerful than solars for that to make sense is sand of another bag ... is that how you say it in english ?, makes more sense spanish. Well I guess the point goes through .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","name":"Cruzwindt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T18:09:48-07:00","id":1244681,"title":"","content":"Then that's where the disagreement lies. Being a PC isn't what makes a character interesting. Having unique traits, views and opinions is what does that. And that means not sweeping entire groups of people together with 'and they basically have no will of their own'.<br /> <br /> How are is a player supposed to make an interesting character out of that without defying the stated trait of 'mindless drone'?<br /> <br /> 2nd ed defining Dragonbloods as being a servant race was a mistake. They aren't, and shouldn't have been. Not if they were also meant to make for interesting antagonists and player characters.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T19:32:38-07:00","id":1244702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244681#post1244681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then that's where the disagreement lies. Being a PC isn't what makes a character interesting. Having unique traits, views and opinions is what does that. And that means not sweeping entire groups of people together with 'and they basically have no will of their own'.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's not what I'm saying at all, being a PC isn't what it makes a character interesting. Being a PC is what makes a character a protagonist ( not necesarily all protagonist are PC, but all PC are protagonists ).<br /> So the realm and the Shogunate shouldn't have existed for putting that many DBs in the same bag ? I think it's a little exagerated to say that just because a person shares some ideologies and is in the same organization as other people they are all the same person or are not individuals. Take for example the Red Cross. Most of the people there are heroes in a more modern sense who help other people, if you live on a disaster area and they arrive to help you are probably gonna consider them heroes despite all of them wanting to help and being members of the same organization.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244681#post1244681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are is a player supposed to make an interesting character out of that without defying the stated trait of 'mindless drone'?</div> </div> </div> </div>By making a compelling story about how a mindless drones discovers his own individuality and stands up against the powers that compel him to obey ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244681#post1244681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2nd ed defining Dragonbloods as being a servant race was a mistake. They aren't, and shouldn't have been. Not if they were also meant to make for interesting antagonists and player characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I find it lorewise acceptable. Also, I don't see the correlation as why a one time servant can't become an antagonist and a player character, that's just a background of it.<br /> For example players can play with Demons if they want, and they are MADE to be servants.<br /> If they choose a human instead of an exalted they are most likely to be servants of a noble.<br /> You can also play like one of the Jade People, most of those are servants too.<br /> Abyssals, Infernals, Alchemicals, all of them are setting servants of a superior power.<br /> Seriously, I don't see the problem with a servant becoming a PC, specially when you don't specifically need to be a servant as per the setting leaves many DBs organizations free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","name":"Cruzwindt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T05:09:07-07:00","id":1244782,"title":"","content":"For one thing it becomes cliche. The goodly drow rebel against his evil kin from the race that if you looked at PCs would seem to be entirely composed of good rebels against their evil kin who ostensibly exist Somewhere. <br /> <br /> For another it spawns stupid arguments of people trying to claim that the dragon blooded should have been interred in purity breeding baby factories and death camps by Solars for their own good, and they would happily go to this fate because they're all indoctrinated in this way, but indoctrination totes isn't brainwashing despite that it in all functional ways is brainwashing if it means every dragon blooded but the rare PC class in the first age would throw away everything and throw themselves into a blender to see if they could become marginally stronger to the tune of roughly 3 motes, in a peaceful age that demanded no significant amount of power where this would become the number one cause of death if implemented<br /> <br /> You would make it so there are two dragon blooded stories. The docile lamb slave and the rebel. 3e permits countless more. Choice is good, especially when it's not a false choice (who would want to play docile lamb slave?).<br /> <br /> Re: &quot;created as a servant race&quot;; you can tell the same story of the dragon blood who Rose up against oppressor without making the state of oppression his Natural and Righteous and Correct state ie being created as a servant race. Having them be the warriors created by the elemental dragons, weaker individually but with the power of numbers behind them, with no assumption of &quot;and they're totes naturally Solar slaves&quot;, makes them more compelling and the potential for individual Solars to have oppressed them and done horrible things in the name of power or the like more offensive to the senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 08-11-2018, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T05:23:32-07:00","id":1244785,"title":"","content":"So I'm going to point out that, in 2nd ed, for most of the First Age most DBs already had Breeding 5 or 6. So for most of the First Age, Purity Crucible Strike wouldn't do anything for most DBs anyway. There was no need to create elaborate and dangerous plans to get DBs to Breeding 5, as they already had it.<br /> <br /> In the High First Age, the Deliberative made it legal to breed with mortals (but most DB families discouraged their kids from doing so anyway), and so for a Dreams of the First Age character, you don't have to have Breeding 5, but you are strongly encouraged to have Breeding 4 (it doesn't even require freebie points). I assume because that's the average Breeding of a DB of that time.<br /> <br /> As allowing them to sully their bloodlines was a recent innovation, I doubt there was much of an incentive for Solars to try and give their DBs +1 Breeding via risky techniques (though DBs might have done it themselves).<br /> <br /> <br /> In 3rd ed... there's no Purity Crucible Strike, so it's irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T07:09:04-07:00","id":1244803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244782#post1244782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one thing it becomes cliche. The goodly drow rebel against his evil kin from the race that if you looked at PCs would seem to be entirely composed of good rebels against their evil kin who ostensibly exist Somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first off, let me say I love that Drizzt reference lol.<br /> Sorry to sound insisting but, cliche is an overused word as of today. People use it as a disqualificative and as something inherently bad. I've seen many cliches like travel back in time to fix things been used in extremely original and fresh ways, that I haven't seen used before ( like for example Tales of Demons and Gods, also big part of the Wuxia genre goes around the cultivation cliche ) . So, just because something is a cliche, it doesn't necessarily makes it bad, nor unoriginal. I'm estimating that it will come the day when we have no more things that we cannot call cliche in some near future.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244782#post1244782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For another it spawns stupid arguments of people trying to claim that the dragon blooded should have been interred in purity breeding baby factories and death camps by Solars for their own good, and they would happily go to this fate because they're all indoctrinated in this way, but indoctrination totes isn't brainwashing despite that it in all functional ways is brainwashing if it means every dragon blooded but the rare PC class in the first age would throw away everything and throw themselves into a blender to see if they could become marginally stronger to the tune of roughly 3 motes, in a peaceful age that demanded no significant amount of power where this would become the number one cause of death if implemented</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm starting to feel that I'm taking the role of 2ed defensor in this thread, which was not what I was thinking when I made it. The original idea was to see if that charm was lorewise acceptable, how it does affect the world around it etc, and talk about fun shenanigans with it, in the end it became a 1ed/3ed vs 2ed. I think I'm going to leave this thread, this is gonna be my final post in it thought I'm going to keep reading it, since my participation in it has been reduced to '' Dude it's not total shit chill '', and I got the feeling we're past the point of actually listen to each other's arguments, so I'm out, it's been fun tho.<br /> <br /> Again, you're ignoring the part where not all dragon blooded in the 1st age 2ed end up like servant slaves. For example, the most influential circle of creation, the one of Deus and The Hierophant, who in 2ed were canonicaly the leaders of the deliberative with 3 Primordial War survivors, had one of it's member's Dragon Blood Gent refuse to serve him and give him the cold shoulder so much, that he decided to leave them alone, making them a free gente that could do whatever they wanted.<br /> You are mixing a lot of things into the bowls, the kind of thing that my OP said, it's something that only the most powerful solars could manage to do, survivors of the thousand struggles era and before. Most solars didn't have that kind of power to do so, and as you say many of those who could do it, ain't nerds sitting on a chair thinking about how to maximize essence.<br /> The part about happily going to do so, can be blame to 2ed social combat system, which I already accepted that's bad, but can be patch a little with a few simple homebrew rules, so I've not had so much trouble with it, maybe I would do a thread about fixes for it. But back to the lore part, why do you act like DBs weren't celestial underlings in the 1ed First Age ? If I recall correctly they were portrayed as so, sure, not all of their roles as underlings were defined so how they enforced celestial rule is left to imagination, but, they were underlings no less, and again, 1ed social system allows brainwashing too, specially against beings incapable of using Sapphire Countermagic, and one could easily homebrew a spell with the same effects as TBotH that needs Adamant countermagic so ....<br /> <br /> Also, you are analyzing the value of breeding merely from the 3 motes output. You are forgetting that in 2ed Breeding allows DBs to use more powerful charms that DBs with lower breeding can't access to. You are also forgetting that breeding allows DBs to breed true, so the million pure DBs you made from the initial experiment, can continue to reproduce without using that method and making many more of them. So I could think of a few reasons in the long term of a thousand years or more of why a Solar would love to make this happen, nvm that others would oppose him and the discontent this would generate.<br /> Also, it was not a peaceful age, unless you want to consider a magical version played out by world shattering beings of the Cold War peaceful.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244782#post1244782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You would make it so there are two dragon blooded stories. The docile lamb slave and the rebel. 3e permits countless more. Choice is good, especially when it's not a false choice (who would want to play docile lamb slave?).<br /> <br /> Re: &quot;created as a servant race&quot;; you can tell the same story of the dragon blood who Rose up against oppressor without making the state of oppression his Natural and Righteous and Correct state ie being created as a servant race. Having them be the warriors created by the elemental dragons, weaker individually but with the power of numbers behind them, with no assumption of &quot;and they're totes naturally Solar slaves&quot;, makes them more compelling and the potential for individual Solars to have oppressed them and done horrible things in the name of power or the like more offensive to the senses.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I've writted above, those weren't the condition of all DBs. And as who would want to play docile lamb slave, you're projecting way into the future and misleading the idea, no one wants to REMAIN a docile lamb slave, but it's a cool story and an underdog position to start with. There are many ways to play that out. Just look Feng Shen Ji, one of the reasons that history captivated me, was because the arrogant prince ended up a slave for a big part of his life at the begginning of the story.<br /> Another example of a DOCILE LAMB slave ? I Shall Seal the Heavens. Meng Hao the protagonist starts as a slave for the reliance sect, and he does so dutifully in order to become a higher rank ( ISSTH is also one of the most famous and well sold novels in modern China )<br /> <br /> Again, the generalization of all DBs are slave it's wrong as per 2ed roles, even if the flawed mechanics may suggest otherwise, sorry if I made you think that.<br /> Also, It would be interesting to hear about the different possibilities you can choose from if you delete the '' DBs were Solar underlings/servants. I don\u00a1't have that many 1ed books, cept the core one, so the few things i know of 1ed's DBs, is that they enforced solar rule back in 1st age, what other sources of the 1st age are in the 1ed that mention them ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","user":"Cruzwindt","date":". 08-11-2018, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12433-cruzwindt","name":"Cruzwindt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T08:15:05-07:00","id":1244823,"title":"","content":"There's a difference between &quot;these weaker Exalts work for me and enforce my will&quot; and &quot;I'm going to force them to breed like rabbits&quot;.<br /> Now Dragon-Blooded have never been mistreated this badly by their Solar canonically in any edition but there's something about the way 2nd edition presented its lore/mechanics (there was a fixation with the original 10,000 Dragon-Blooded who apparently could just be told to have a massive multi-generational orgy and produce an army and notions of lost 'purity') that kept leading to players having ideas like this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T09:05:49-07:00","id":1244831,"title":"","content":"To be fair, I don't recall it saying they were <i>told </i>to have a massive orgy. <br /> <br /> They just... did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T16:19:08-07:00","id":1244964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cruzwindt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244803#post1244803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, first off, let me say I love that Drizzt reference lol.<br /> Sorry to sound insisting but, cliche is an overused word as of today. People use it as a disqualificative and as something inherently bad. I've seen many cliches like travel back in time to fix things been used in extremely original and fresh ways, that I haven't seen used before ( like for example Tales of Demons and Gods, also big part of the Wuxia genre goes around the cultivation cliche ) . So, just because something is a cliche, it doesn't necessarily makes it bad, nor unoriginal. I'm estimating that it will come the day when we have no more things that we cannot call cliche in some near future.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What you're describing is called a trope. Tropes are story elements that get reused over and over because it turns out that stories often naturally gravitate towards using them. This can be good or bad. Cliches are story elements that get used over and over because it's easier for the author than thinking their work through and coming up with their own ideas instead. This can be neutral (if done to move the actual main plot along instead of bogging it down with side bits) or bad (when it diminishes the main themes).<br /> <br /> In this case, as we are dealing with a group of people intended to be used by STs and players to fill their story with interesting characters, using a blanket generalisation to define them all is using a cliche, not a trope. It was done to reduce the effort of fleshing out the first age, but as it was meant to be an idea pool for players to build characters out of, that was a bad move. If you want to encourage creativity, you don't start by offering a setting full of bland filler. The story didn't call for this, the readers didn't call for this, but the authors did it because it was easier. Thus, it's a cliche (and a bad one), not a trope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":12735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","user":"BjornTheFellhanded","date":". 08-11-2018, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T18:37:08-07:00","id":1245011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1244831#post1244831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, I don't recall it saying they were <i>told </i>to have a massive orgy.<br /> <br /> They just... did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking back this is the case but looking back... jesus fucking christ.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoEP: Dragon-Blooded</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the entire first year of their existence, the lives of those who composed the Dragon-Blooded Host were more akin to never-ending orgies than anything resembling warfare. Solar generals found themselves fitting combat training in between the Terrestrials\u2019 extended bouts of rutting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T09:28:05-07:00","id":1245126,"title":"","content":"See guys?<br /> <br /> This is why the bronze faction was right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T15:24:30-07:00","id":1245201,"title":"","content":"Eh, the bronze faction can have plenty to be right about without 2e-based mass-breeding plans (thank all the wisdom of 3e that it made &quot;mass-breed DBs!&quot; not just impractical but impossible. Get a bunch of Terrestrial woman to put out 10,000 babies in a year and you have 10,000 mortal babies [and probably pissed off elemental demigoddesses]). Solars going to petty wars deploying terrible sorceries and weaponry that creates horrible widespread misery and death and leaves lands uninhabitable all because of their ego is plenty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T15:34:45-07:00","id":1245209,"title":"","content":"Eh, you'd get one or two deebs out of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T10:01:30-07:00","id":1245539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1245011#post1245011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking back this is the case but looking back... jesus fucking christ.<br /> <br /> [ plus a quote ]<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure mileage may vary, but I thought that was a good story element to DBs. It struck me as being very Gaian, very primal and instinctive and made sense for a group of supernaturals who (as a category) gained power by multiplying. And best of all, it made their origin entirely distinct from all the Celestials, which was a benefit to their story too.<br /> <br /> If that was a source of friction with everybody else, so much the better as story fodder. <br /> <br /> My headcanon DBs retain that particular instinct. Civilized DBs constrain and channel their enthusiasm through the expectations of society, with greater or lesser success. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T13:57:36-07:00","id":1245625,"title":"","content":"Well, the year-long orgy was due to there being a huge gender imbalance in the initial ten thousand to exploit a quirk of biology that progenitive essence removes. Now that the initial numbers were more or less even you could say that those first dragon blooded did pair up quickly and bring about the second generation in the first year, without the need for massive orgies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T14:18:55-07:00","id":1245636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1245539#post1245539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And best of all, it made their origin entirely distinct from all the Celestials...</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Distinct</i>, though, does not equal <i>good</i>. 2e Infernals were <i>distinct</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T14:20:46-07:00","id":1245639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1245539#post1245539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My headcanon DBs retain that particular instinct. Civilized DBs constrain and channel their enthusiasm through the expectations of society, with greater or lesser success.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really headcanon, MoEP: Dragon-Blooded infers as such and it's part of what fuels plans like the one in the OP.<br /> &quot;Oh yeah Dragon-Blooded are like hypersexual they won't have any serious issue with being ordered to procreate with complete strangers.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T08:19:08-07:00","id":1245887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1245639#post1245639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not really headcanon, MoEP: Dragon-Blooded infers as such and it's part of what fuels plans like the one in the OP.<br /> &quot;Oh yeah Dragon-Blooded are like hypersexual they won't have any serious issue with being ordered to procreate with complete strangers.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed on both points. I was just pointing out that I liked the Ex1 excerpt because it added story differentiation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hm. An interesting story might include a jaded DB as the only one capable of breaking the Lover c.i.t.r.o.t.'s heart. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T08:44:45-07:00","id":1245894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1245887#post1245887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just pointing out that I liked the Ex1 excerpt because it added story differentiation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:31:19-07:00","id":1245916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1245539#post1245539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It struck me as being very Gaian, very primal and instinctive</div> </div> </div> </div>Even within the terms of the Five Elemental Dragons being Gaia's Primordial souls, these things have precious little to do with the Terrestrial Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">made sense for a group of supernaturals who (as a category) gained power by multiplying.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand &quot;making sense&quot; is no more an excuse for something being terribly crass and unpleasant for little to no benefit than &quot;historical accuracy&quot; is.<br /> <br /> On the other, there's something dubious in the idea of it making sense, considering typical human social models.<br /> <br /> {checks excerpt again}<br /> <br /> You know, it's actually really dumb even in its own terms, because it's somehow trying to reconcile an idea of them being extremely fertile with the notion that it took a whole year for a ratio of one man to get nine women pregnant. Like, the &quot;Solar generals&quot; had a hard time getting them into consistent training regimens for all of the fucking that was going on, even though surely within the first few months there must have been several thousand women that were already pregnant?<br /> <br /> \u2026 Oh wait, no it was <i>ninety</i> nine women per man. Hmm, that makes its logic of the length of time it took a bit more plausible, but is still overlooking the idea that within just a few weeks there should have been a sizable number that had gotten that business over and done with.<br /> <br /> Mind, I'm running on an assumption that orgies are not particularly efficient as means of ensuring that people become pregnant, especially when it's supposed to be a ratio of one man to ninety nine women (if nothing else, it's got to be kind of boring to be among those several dozen women that are not anywhere near the man, unless it's dependent on the logic of the game's puerile &quot;everybody is bisexual&quot; phase), so I'm presuming that it could be imagined to take time because each man would have to impregnate each woman one at a time... which should still logically leave a lot of women that are waiting their turn free to engage in training. On the other hand, if an orgy <i>is</i> a reasonably functional way of winding up with people that are pregnant (which still needs to account for the mechanics of such an orgy when there is such a massive gender disparity), then we get back to the question of why it took so damn long.<br /> <br /> Well look at that; it's the kind of thing that appears superficially clever when you just pop it out there, and kind falls apart in every respect when you take a couple of minutes to think about it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And best of all, it made their origin entirely distinct from all the Celestials, which was a benefit to their story too.</div> </div> </div> </div>What other origins?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My headcanon DBs retain that particular instinct. Civilized DBs constrain and channel their enthusiasm through the expectations of society, with greater or lesser success.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Are you saying that you picture them as having sex drives that are so high that they're actually a distraction from doing other things?<br /> <br /> My God, the most fecund life forms in the world can effectively do things besides constantly have sex with one another.<br /> <br /> I'm not even going to touch that comment on a Dragon Blood being able to exert influence over a Deathlord through the edifying power of his magic cock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:35:32-07:00","id":1245919,"title":"","content":"They're so fertile they even multiply the word count!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:48:54-07:00","id":1245927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1245919#post1245919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're so fertile they even multiply the word count!</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that made me grin a little bit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:50:27-07:00","id":1245928,"title":"","content":"What if... there was a better way that got everyone's attention? Secret martial arts are supposed to be secret after all.<br /> <br /> In the warm seas of the Southwest on the continent of the Caul stand Manses blessed by the long-ago presence of Gaia. Widely celebrated were their powers to bolster nesting Dragons; many a mother later rejoiced at the elemental power bursting from her child. But even a gift as holy and pure as the Dragons' blessing can arouse envy and fear. In times of peace and security, their powers were restricted by bureaucracy and process. In times of war and instability, they were exploited by the local ruler, handed out as favors to the Dragon-Blooded who chose to serve her. Amidst the battles, many such Manses were destroyed or lost, never to be rebuilt into their former glory unless the Shining Answer returns the Green Mother to Creation. The remaining are squabbled over in the Age of Sorrows as they have been in every age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:54:14-07:00","id":1245932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1245927#post1245927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, that made me grin a little bit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><b>[Harmonious Forum Viewpoint Attitude] </b><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:56:41-07:00","id":1245936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1245639#post1245639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not really headcanon, MoEP: Dragon-Blooded infers as such and it's part of what fuels plans like the one in the OP.<br /> &quot;Oh yeah Dragon-Blooded are like hypersexual they won't have any serious issue with being ordered to procreate with complete strangers.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>A question kind of begged by the 2e origin of DBs is that there needed to be litereal armies of DBs, and that the ones that the Dragons Chose to begin withe re insufficient for whatever else armies of the Exalted needed.<br /> <br /> I mean, going by <b>Games of Divinity</b>, I got this gist that the First Generation went right to war with the other Chosen. Them being able to ahve kids is a thing with a neat side effect, not a planned factor to inflate their nubmers even greater. The original set as what the Exalted Host needed. This fits also a bit with 1e and 3e's take taht Dragon-Blooded were usually high ranking officers and lieutenants, not line footsoldiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T10:18:18-07:00","id":1245943,"title":"","content":"Headcanon?<br /> <br /> Gaia took a million humans, took them apart, wove the dragonblooded exaltation into them, and then placed them on the ground. <br /> <br /> They say that even now, in the age of sorrows, the sheer geomantic power brought about by a million dragonblooded taking their first breathe can wreck an entire direction...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T05:46:04-07:00","id":1246279,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;side effect&quot; is the wrong word. They knew that the dragonblooded exaltations would be non-reincarnating (possibly a trade-off for making so many) so they needed them to have some means of replenishing their numbers.<br /> <br /> But, much like they didn't intend the celestials to immediately begin reincarnating, they likely didn't intend the deebs to immediately set about producing the next generation.<br /> <br /> &quot;guys you live for 300 years now, take your time.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T07:38:03-07:00","id":1246328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1246279#post1246279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think &quot;side effect&quot; is the wrong word. They knew that the dragonblooded exaltations would be non-reincarnating (possibly a trade-off for making so many) so they needed them to have some means of replenishing their numbers.<br /> <br /> But, much like they didn't intend the celestials to immediately begin reincarnating, they likely didn't intend the deebs to immediately set about producing the next generation.<br /> <br /> &quot;guys you live for 300 years now, take your time.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not. It was a design cosntraint due to the Elemental Dragons being &quot;the weakest among the gods&quot; in a context that seems to have &quot;god&quot; be different from other spirits (&quot;god&quot; as broad term for that sort of being wasn't until GoD, and the Introduction was written much earlier). In a 3e context, it's probably less that an dmore just...that's how the Elemental Dragons Exalt people. No real need for purpose or design I think because it's more about inherent nature.<br /> <br /> I will note, <b>Games of Diinity </b>does use the term soldier, but I think it needs to ahve a couple caveats. 1) As one of the first bits written for the line, I do kind of wonder if GCG had thought of the populaiton of Exalts much yet. There was an even earlier design pass where Exalts were roughly equal afterall. 2) It was likely written with a different sense of assumed Dragon-Blooded power, as shown by other piece sof early 1e fiction.<br /> <br /> That also said, the rates we see Dragon-Blooded reproduction and the scales involved, we're not sure the immediacy of the war, but I doubt it was slow. I'm generally fine with there being 10,000 Dragons to start with (it's a cool number) and that the Dragons just get played as being pretty damne dmighty in htemselves to Exalt that many, just also very different to do so in such a way. The population of DBs hasn't ever gotten much more than today, mostly because there's constraints of Progenitive Essence, the last eight centuries have been relatively peaceful for th world, and I like the idea introduced in 3e where Dragon-Blooded aren't obligated to follow Celestials and never were, instead being assets to be garnered rather than servants to be ordered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T09:08:35-07:00","id":1246352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244197-2e-purity-crucible-strike-how-comes-dragon-bloods-ain-t-pure?p=1245916#post1245916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(if nothing else, it's got to be kind of boring to be among those several dozen women that are not anywhere near the man, unless it's dependent on the logic of the game's puerile &quot;everybody is bisexual&quot; phase)</div> </div> </div> </div>This may shed a little light on that. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoEP: Dragon-Blooded</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Mortal women might have been forbidden to the lusty Dragon-Blooded men but everyone (and every<i>thing</i>) else was fair game, and historians claim that the frequency of homosexual relations among the Dragon-Blooded dates back to this period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit: You can't see it in the quote but they actually italicised the thing part of everything in the book... that's actually kind of amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 08-15-2018, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T10:08:22-07:00","id":1246368,"title":"","content":"Ah. <br /> <br /> Let me tell you of the romance between an earth aspect and a mountain...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}